('physics-si-units-01','physics','mechanics','Units and measurements','SI units','Which is the SI unit of force?','["joule","newton","watt","pascal"]',1,'The derived SI unit of force is the newton, N=kg·m·s⁻².','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Physics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('physics-significant-figures-01','physics','mechanics','Units and measurements','Significant figures','How many significant figures are in 0.00450?','["2","3","4","5"]',1,'Leading zeros are not significant, while the trailing zero after the decimal is; 4,5,0 gives three.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Physics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
