('physics-vernier-screw-gauge-01','physics','mechanics','Units and measurements','Vernier calipers and screw gauge','The least count of a screw gauge equals:','["pitch × number of circular divisions","pitch / number of circular divisions","number of divisions / pitch","pitch + number of divisions"]',1,'One circular-division rotation advances the screw by pitch divided by the number of divisions.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Physics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('physics-one-dimensional-motion-01','physics','mechanics','Kinematics','Motion in one dimension','A body starts from rest with constant acceleration 2 m/s². What is its speed after 5 s?','["2 m/s","5 m/s","10 m/s","25 m/s"]',2,'v=u+at=0+2×5=10 m/s.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Physics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('physics-relative-velocity-01','physics','mechanics','Kinematics','Vectors and relative velocity','Two cars move east at 20 m/s and 12 m/s. The velocity of the first relative to the second is:','["8 m/s east","8 m/s west","32 m/s east","zero"]',0,'For motion along the same line, v₁₂=v₁−v₂=8 m/s east.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Physics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('physics-projectile-motion-01','physics','mechanics','Kinematics','Projectile motion','Ignoring air resistance, which component of a projectile’s velocity remains constant?','["vertical component","horizontal component","speed","both components"]',1,'Gravity acts vertically, so horizontal acceleration is zero and horizontal velocity stays constant.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Physics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('physics-uniform-circular-motion-01','physics','mechanics','Kinematics','Uniform circular motion','For uniform circular motion of speed v and radius r, centripetal acceleration is:','["vr","v/r","v²/r","r²/v"]',2,'The inward radial acceleration has magnitude v²/r.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Physics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
